Fixed in 0a4ce01fe5c22a92c0a9ddaa69c0cca7c1d5a87a.

The new show of a held id now records the holder it took the id from and what it took. If it throws or answers `failed` while it still holds the id, it hands both back and reinstates that holder, which stays clickable.

Covered by new tests in `okr/desktop/test/alerts.test.cjs`:
- a sync throw and an async `failed`: the earlier alert is clickable and opens once;
- a click while the replacement is pending is not undone by its later failure;
- a failure of a show no longer holding the id (a third show took it) changes nothing;
- a show whose own notification failed is passed over on the way back;
- an alert really let go (dismissed) is never given back.

Making the failure path always release fails 3 of them.

